# =============================================================================
# .gitignore — TRACE-Kin / PSICHIC_Kin
# Public surface only. Heavy outputs (model weights, per-sample interpretations,
# job logs) live on HPC and should never be committed.
# =============================================================================

# --- Local archive (kept on disk for reference, not for public history) ----
to_remove/

# --- Python build / cache --------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo
*.egg
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/

# --- Virtualenvs / package managers ----------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/
.env

# --- Editor / OS clutter ---------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
.cursor/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# --- Notebook clutter ------------------------------------------------------
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- Model weights & preprocessing caches ---------------------------------
# Model weights are large and produced by HPC training runs; checkpoint paths
# are documented in PROJECT.md but the files themselves never enter git.
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.bin

# --- LSF job outputs (TRACKED, not ignored) -------------------------------
# *.stdout / *.stderr / *.smoke.stdout / *.smoke.stderr from run_benchmark.lsf
# and the array LSFs are intentionally kept under version control so the HPC
# (which runs the jobs and writes the logs) can push results to GitHub for the
# local clone to pull. Workflow: HPC `git add *.stdout *.stderr && git push`,
# local `git pull`. Watch repo size — if a single log file exceeds ~50 MB,
# truncate it on HPC before committing or move that file to Git LFS.

# --- Generated figures (regenerated locally from clean CSV) ---------------
# Keep figures/output/ out of git so the repo stays small. Reviewers can
# regenerate on demand: `python figures/generate_figures.py`.
figures/output/

# --- Heavy result trees ----------------------------------------------------
# These directories live on HPC; they're listed here in case anyone rsync's
# them down for local inspection — they should not be committed.
TRACE_Kin_Results/
TRACE_Kin_Results_v1_repro/
TRACE_Kin_Results_v2/

# --- Runtime artifacts -----------------------------------------------------
submitted_jobs.txt
data/benchmark/_smoke/

# --- Current result tree ---------------------------------------------------
# The SLURM launchers default RESULT_PATH to "$REPO/results/...", i.e. INSIDE
# the repo, so the whole run output would otherwise be staged. The
# TRACE_Kin_Results*/ patterns above only match the older naming.
# Covers: save_model_seed*/, test_prediction_seed*.csv, full_result-*.txt and
# the interpretation_result_seed*/PAIR_*/ trees.
results/

# --- Per-pair interpretation output (wherever it is written) ---------------
# virtual_screening(save_interpret=True) writes ONE DIRECTORY PER PAIR, each
# containing protein.csv / ligand.csv / fingerprint.npy. That is thousands of
# tiny files for a normal test split — it exhausts inode quota on HPC and must
# never enter git. Regenerate on demand with
# `python inference/predict.py --interpret_dir <dir>`.
interpretation_result_seed*/
**/PAIR_*/

# --- NumPy artifacts -------------------------------------------------------
# fingerprint.npy (per-pair interaction fingerprints, data_utils.py) and
# v5t_features.npz (extracted deep features, v6b_xgboost_on_v5t_features.py).
*.npy
*.npz

# --- Dataset splits / feature tables --------------------------------------
# Datasets live outside the repo ($dir_path/kinetic_dataset/...). This is a
# guard in case a datafolder is ever placed inside the tree; the protein.pt /
# ligand.pt / molformer_emb.pt caches beside them are already covered by *.pt.
# NOTE: deliberately NOT ignoring *.csv — trace_doc/kinetic_regress_benchmark.csv
# and data/benchmark/*.csv are tracked ground truth.
*.parquet

# =============================================================================
# Explicitly tracked artifacts (DO commit these — listed for reviewer clarity):
#   - data/benchmark/kinetic_regress_benchmark_clean.csv
#   - data/benchmark/normalization_log.md
#   - data/benchmark/significance.csv
#   - data/benchmark/trace_kin_v2_results.csv (after rerun completes)
#   - data/benchmark/promotion_gate_decision.md
#   - data/benchmark/improvement_summary.md
#   - data/benchmark/tables/*.md and *.tex
# =============================================================================
